      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I hear the deep pain and exhaustion in your words about feeling like a \"leftover piece\" that disrupts the peace you wish to give them. While surviving a tragedy is incredibly hard, the desire to help a loved one heal does not make you a \"shadow\" that you should erase to do it.\nI know this is not a \"solution\" the way you think, and I hope you know I am here to support you not in ending your life, but in finding a way to care for yourself and help through this endless process.\nPlease consider talking to a counselor who can help you find hope, as these kinds of thoughts can sometimes be a symptom of severe grief or depression that needs professional support.\nJust know that your life is a gift to the world and to your family, and it is possible to find a way to help them let go without ending your own life.",
